sec.p:
After identification of the base PK model, participant baseline characteristics (age, race, body weight [BW], body mass index [BMI], body surface area [BSA]), sex and cancer type were considered for evaluation as covariates on model parameters (clearance [CL], central volume of distribution [V

c
], inter‐compartmental clearance [Q] and peripheral volume of distribution [V

p
]) to explain variability in ginisortamab serum concentrations. Dose was tested as a potential covariate graphically; however, because of the lack of any sign of relationship between dose and any of the PK parameters, no formal test was performed in NONMEM. Covariates that showed a correlation with the random effects and had possible clinical relevance were further evaluated for inclusion and retained if there was a statistically significant change in OFV using a stepwise approach with forward inclusion (P < .01) and backward elimination (P < .001).
